00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.190
- My parents met at a movie theater.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.920
My mom was working there
and my dad came in,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.330
and he just had a crush on her.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.420
So he'd always keep coming
back and just watching movies.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.024
- That's really wholesome.
- Yeah.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:32.857
(group chuckles)

00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:34.140
- My dad was a tennis coach

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.670
at University of Central Missouri,

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.280
and my mother was an international
student learning tennis.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.870
So that's how they met.
- International student.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.134
You threw that in there.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.030
(group chuckles)
Okay, I see it.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.790
- She said, "Oh, you mentioned
international student,"

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.470
so I thought she was targeting me,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.800
so I thought, "Mm, okay.
Maybe she's the mole."

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.840
- My parents met in grad school.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.520
They both went to Georgia Tech.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.150
My dad's from Georgia, but
my mom immigrated from France

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.740
to go to grad school in the U.S.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.800
So they just met each other
in the engineering department.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.510
- My parents met at a barbecue.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.860
My dad was in the military,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.890
so he was in Osan Air Base in South Korea.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.480
And my mom was at that barbecue

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.800
because she lived near Osan.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.730
She would tell me about it.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.800
She was like, "Yeah, I thought
Americans were really weird

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.950
because your dad showed up
in shorts and flip flops

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.440
and a button up tee
with a Russian bear hat

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.700
and it was winter."
(group chuckles)

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.027
And I was just like,

00:02:22.027 --> 00:02:23.280
"And then you ended up marrying him."

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.080
She's like, "Yeah." (chuckles)
- How nice.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.080
My parents met in LA, which
is like the mixing pot.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.660
So makes sense, I guess, yeah.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.880
- She had said that her
parents had met in LA,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.740
but she didn't really elaborate on that.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.690
Everyone else had kind
of gone into more detail

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.560
about their parents,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.450
and I felt like that was a little strange.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:43.083
- My parents are both from Arizona.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:49.070
They met, I would say at
a bar, I think. (titters)

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.883
So yeah, my mom is from the
Navajo Nation reservation.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.199
