00:08:23.477 --> 00:08:26.102
(group exclaims)

00:08:26.102 --> 00:08:28.299
- I'm Lebanese, Arab, Middle Eastern,

00:08:28.299 --> 00:08:30.570
(chuckles) which is
technically white in the US.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.430
People from North Africa, so like Egypt,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.470
Tunisia, Algeria, et cetera,

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.420
and people from the Middle
East are considered white

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.380
on the U.S. census.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.070
So it really goes to show
how arbitrary (chuckles)

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.210
the term white is,

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:44.280
in the ways in which
it's applied to people.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.110
- I always think it's
silly that on the census

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.990
it's Black, white, Asian.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:51.030
The categories are so limited,

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.620
and so when I'm doing the census,

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.470
I just put white because
I look like I'm white.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.790
It just goes to show you

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.120
that no matter what somebody looks like,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.680
you could be biracial, like your hair.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.230
I would've thought, "Okay, I
could believe that you're mixed

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.270
'cause you have the curly
hair," but you never know.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.363
- Yeah.

